WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.950
If something bounces back, the speeds add.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:10.510
In at 12 metres per second, out at 8, that's a change of 20, not 4.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.170
Put a negative sign on the velocity that goes the other way, and the maths

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.390
does it for you.

